    "explanation": "Both sides agree on the decisive arithmetic and so do I, so this is decided rather than escalated.\n\nDid the driver arrive? Yes. EV-TRIP-00203 records the driver 'arrived' event at 19:41:35, and EV-GPS-00203 (weight 1.0, 60 fixes, 100% coverage, no gaps) places him inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius from 19:41:20, with 21 consecutive qualifying fixes whose reported accuracy is 5-11 m (well inside the 25 m filter) and a closest approach of 18.7 m to the pin. POL-NS-01 limbs (a) and (b) are met. The arrival marker is not false: he was stationary at 0.0 kph at 18.7 m, so neither the 300 m distance trigger nor the 15 kph motion trigger in POL-NS-05 fires, and no false-arrival entry is recorded against him.\n\nWhy the fee still fails. POL-NS-01 is deliberately conjunctive, and limb (c) requires a continuous in-geofence dwell of 300 seconds for a STANDARD pickup, measured from the first qualifying in-geofence fix and not from the 'arrived' tap. The driver's own trace measures a single unbroken run of 195 seconds (19:41:20 to 19:44:35) against that 300-second minimum - a shortfall of 105 seconds - and he cancelled at 19:44:40. Limb (c) is not met and limb (d)'s requirement that termination come at or after the dwell elapsed fails with it. POL-NS-06 then makes the result automatic: the cancellation fee is not chargeable and is refunded in full. Accumulation under POL-NS-06 limb (i) is unavailable on this trace - there is only one in-geofence run to sum, and the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00203-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT), so no advisory permits summing and none exonerates anyone.\n\nPOL-NS-07 cannot pay the driver. The 80 percent compensation is payable only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, and it is not; POL-NS-06 states expressly that a shortfall yields the full refund and no driver compensation.\n\nPOL-NS-04 does not carry this ruling in either direction. The rider's message at 19:42:50 was answered by the driver at 19:44:31, 101 seconds later and therefore inside the clause's 120-second window, so limb (b) fails and the clause does not apply. Separately, her rider track inside EV-GPS-00203 (all 60 fixes between 36.4 m and 51.6 m of the pin, stationary throughout 19:43:12 to 19:46:00) affirmatively places her at the pickup point, consistent with her account of a slow block lift and not with an absent no-show.\n\nNo escalation arises. The deciding fact - the 195-second dwell - is carried by EV-GPS-00203 at weight 1.0, so POL-GEN-02(2) caps confidence at 1.0 and POL-NS-09(a) is not engaged. Both profiles show disputes_with_counterparty_90d = 0, so POL-NS-09(c) is not met; rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 1, below the 3 that POL-NS-09(d) requires; the POL-NS-07 anti-farming test does not trip (2 no-show terminations against 131 completed trips, a rate of 0.015, below both the count of 4 and the 0.08 ratio); no two admissible artifacts contradict each other on arrival, dwell or rider presence; and the deciding fact does not rest solely on an impaired artifact.\n\nOn the evidence itself: the chat log EV-CHAT-00203 is impaired at weight 0.85 with issue LANGUAGE_AMBIGUITY, because the rider's 'wait ah, i coming liao' is genuinely contestable between 'I am on my way' and 'I am already here'. The finding does not rest on it - both the dwell and the timeline rest on the unimpaired GPS trace - so the discount does not change the outcome. The fare breakdown reconciles exactly: SGD 4.00 is the greater of the STANDARD zone-class fee (4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (4.00), so there is no POL-NS-08(d) defect, and base fare, distance, time, waiting, platform fee, surcharges, tolls and promo are all zero.\n\nOutcome for both parties: the whole contested SGD 4.00 cancellation fee is returned to the rider. The driver receives no compensation, because the waiting period the fee is consideration for was never completed. No referral is made, since no clause on these facts produces one."
  },
